ry":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.5.dev4.official [209a446e3]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.dev4\n\n### Issue description (+Steps to reproduce)\n\nI encountered a rather interesting bug. When I was creating new scenes by saving nodes into separate scenes, everything worked fine - until an error appeared in the menuMainSettings scene. That’s the scene I was using to extract nodes into new scenes. Apparently, when I changed the class type, something went wrong - though I didn’t realize what exactly, everything seemed like usual.\n\nBecause of this, the project stopped working. Then, through the error message, I managed to open this file:\n`res://scenes/mainMenu/menuMainSettings.tscn::GDScript_evgvs`.\n\nIt turned out to be a full copy of a .gd file. After cleaning it up, everything started working again. But I became curious: how do you delete this, and what even is it?\n\nI didn’t see this script in the scene tree - as far as I understand, it’s something internal to the scene. In the editor, it's displayed as a gear icon with no fill. Also, after cleaning up the file and trying to restart, I couldn’t save this script anymore - and without saving, it just vanished from the editor.\n\nSo yeah, strange bug. 😐\nI just wanted to share it in case others run into the same thing. I can’t provide more details. As far as I understand, I wasn’t supposed to even see GDScript_evgvs - if I’m wrong, please correct me.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n--","closed_by":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https